      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#1–#2 · CW11 paraphrase with paragraph locators; the quilt's assumption-of correction (human-amplified: yes)",
          "title": "The incarnation–Assumption chiasm",
          "italic": "The chiasm demonstrates the crossed reading: what a pole does and the field it bear produce different valences — and the return must retain the body that bore the relation.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "Two directions. First, the matrix receives the Logos into bodily life: divine Word through a body which bears it. In return, that body is itself received — assumption-of, not ascent-away-from: return bears what made manifestation possible. If only a general feminine principle entered the account, the particular body would disappear where recognition claims completion. The chiasm names the crossed readings: articulation, differentiation, explication give 1–2–3 a masculine operation; receiving,",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "containing, reflecting and gathering give 4–5–0 a feminine one — while the older assignment associates matter with the feminine, mind with the masculine. Both relations are held as the object of inquiry — symbolic assignments being developed, not determinations of what men and women are. Jung's attributed sequence runs from Proverbs' wisdom through the Second Eve to the Assumption discussion; the proposed Sophia–Logos–Śakti three-office distribution is assistant elaboration (human-amplified: no).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "occ",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "Occurrences: the receiving and the received body (#1); the crossed masculine/feminine operations (#2); Jung's §§609–628, 746–757 as attributed paraphrase (#1); the perfection/completeness difficulty (#1).",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.78,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
      ],
