      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#3–#4 · Taylor's explicit corrections (human-amplified: yes); A11/C49; A16; A13/C50",
          "title": "Wheels, wings and the eagle's signed power",
          "italic": "The corrections demonstrate authorship governing pattern: a pleasing reading is revised against the native relations, and the eagle's shared body is asked which operation it carries.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "The wheels give the crossing a second form: the sequence 0/1 → 1/0 → (0/1)/(1/0) — a first orientation meets its inverse, their relation explicit; the outer slash divides no numerical quantities. A wheel changes orientation while its whole form persists; two wheels bear conjugate orientations, not becoming independent sources. The seraphic forms articulate orientation as sixfold and its primed counterpart, each retaining the blocks — the dialogue's first vertical",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "pairing is corrected: 2↔5 and 3↔0 rejected, only 1↔4 of it holding; the native complementary folds are 0↔5, 1↔4, 2↔3. The eagle changes the question: the wheels' equations and a 1/1 reconciliation are refused it; the retained form is (-1)/(+1) — addition cancels, each subtraction appropriates, and sign does not fix moral worth. Isaiah's wings and Ezekiel's wheels remain a distinct textual proposal needing its own object witness.",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "occ",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "Occurrences: the wheel sequence (#3); the corrected wing pairings (#3); the eagle's signed-power correction (#4); the scriptural invocation kept as proposal (#3).",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.78,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
      ],
